title: Threats
subtitle: There are other ways to win a vote.
view-if: congress = 1 and congress_closing = 0 and congress_used_walkout = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.congress_used_walkout = 1;
Q.sys_outcome = 0;
!}
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: congress

= Threats

The [+ congress_rival_name +] are counting on the delegates who would rather lose a vote than split the party. That works both ways. A threat, made in time, can be worth a dozen speeches. A threat that fails has to be carried out, or swallowed.

- @walkout: Threaten that our delegates will walk out.
- @resign: Threaten to resign the Zentrale.
- @expel: Warn that those who defy the congress will be expelled.
- @none: No threats. Let the congress decide.

@walkout
subtitle: Many delegates will not risk a split. If we lose anyway, the party will pay for it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.congress_walkout = 1;
RG.congress.sway(0.07 + Math.random() * 0.03);
RG.congress.bitter(4);
!}

We let it be known that if the congress votes against us, our delegates will leave the hall and the party with it. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates decide that the party matters more than the motion. ?]

@resign
subtitle: The loyal districts rally round the Zentrale. Costs a little Unity.
view-if: congress_backing_is_lead = 1
on-arrival: {!
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    if (Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] >= 50) {
        RG.congress.convert(d, 0.15);
    }
}
RG.congress.sway(0.02);
Q.unity -= 3;
!}

The Zentrale will not carry out a policy it believes is wrong: if the motion falls, the Zentrale goes. The districts that trust it close ranks. Our side now has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall.

@expel
subtitle: Frightens the weaker delegates. The rivals will hate us for it.
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.sway(0.05);
RG.congress.bitter(6);
if (Q.congress_rival && Q[Q.congress_rival + '_satisfaction'] !== undefined) {
    Q[Q.congress_rival + '_satisfaction'] -= 8;
}
Q.unity -= 4;
!}

The Zentrale reminds the congress what discipline means: the minority submits, or leaves. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates decide not to be the minority. ?]

@none
subtitle: Calms the hall. Raises Unity a little.
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.bitter(-2);
Q.unity += 2;
!}

We make no threats. Several delegates of the [+ congress_rival_name +] say, in the corridor, that this is the first decent thing the Zentrale has done all week.
